# `ldconfig -p -C` on a cache that does not exist. The reference's wrapper script starts the program as
# `/sbin/ldconfig.real`, which is the name in its message; the spec writes `<program>` there (§31.2 Failure), so this
# transcript maps that one name to `ldconfig`, the name libniji's side is started with.
name: ldconfig -p on a missing cache prints the open failure and exits 1
clause: s31_2_f_1
command: ldconfig
env: LC_ALL=C
arg: -p
arg: -C
arg: @ROOT@/no-such-cache
normalise: /sbin/ldconfig.real => ldconfig
status: exit 1
stdout:
stderr:
| ldconfig: Can't open cache file @ROOT@/no-such-cache
| : No such file or directory
